      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this will work for now, but I\u0027ll make a note here, since it might matter if you wanted to emulate the early stages of attaching or test how we implement CC toggling. I\u0027m not sure this is quite the right way to describe/handle this concept.\n\nAt the time of connection, if the partner is acting as Source, it will be presenting Rp on both CC lines. If it is Sink, it will be presenting Rd on both lines. The cable will physically hide one of the lines and maybe present Ra. At that time, our side will either be acting as Source and presenting Rp on both CC lines or acting as Sink and presenting Rd.\n\nIf we\u0027re presenting Rp, we can\u0027t distinguish between Rp and Open. If we\u0027re presenting Rd, we can\u0027t distinguish between Rd or Ra and Open. So those conditions get reported as Open in our CC_STATUS.\n\nThis code doesn\u0027t seem to handle the Rp/Rp (Source/Source) or Rd/Rd (Sink/Sink) cases. (I take it that they are not expected.) It\u0027s also making the decision based on the partner\u0027s role, when it should technically be based on our own role (in ROLE_CONTROL.CC* and CC_STATUS.ConnectResult).\n\nIf you only want to handle stable Source/Sink connections, this should work. If you want to test code that handles unusable connections or DRPAutotoggle (or sets up the TCPC to handle those things), you might need to make this more elaborate.",
